    "declared_proposition": "Let r be the initial number of accelerated Collatz valuations equal to one and let b>=2 be the next valuation. If b>=r+2, then T^(r+1)(n)<n for every positive odd n>1 realizing that word. These words have exact relative odd-Haar mass 2/3.",
    "mathematical_argument": "Write n+1=2^(r+1)q with q odd. Then T^(r+1)(n)=(3^(r+1)q-1)/2^(b-1). The worst case is b=r+2. Descent reduces to q(4^(r+1)-3^(r+1))>2^(r+1)-1. For r>=1 this follows from 4^m-3^m>=4^(m-1)>=2^m with m=r+1. For r=0 it is strict unless q=1, which is exactly n=1. The word 1^r,b has relative odd-Haar mass 2^(-(r+b)). Summing b>=r+2 and r>=0 gives sum_r 2^(-r)sum_(b>=r+2)2^(-b)=2/3.",
